# Provenance-marker hygiene (feat-foundry-provenance-marker-hygiene, ER #180).
#
# The build-provenance marker is tracked-yet-gitignored (see .gitignore) — committed on a feature
# branch, but never re-created from a clean checkout. Without this line, `git merge origin/main` on
# a feature branch auto-merges the marker to main's version WITHOUT flagging a conflict, silently
# replacing the branch's own `spec_ref` / `contract_sha256` with the previously-merged atom's marker
# — the merge gate then validates the WRONG contract (CHECK-1/1b/4/7 all key off it). `merge=ours`
# selects git's built-in `ours` merge driver for this path, so a merge KEEPS the current branch's
# version instead of auto-merging the other side (gitattributes(5), "Defining a custom merge
# driver" — the built-in `ours` driver; no `.gitattributes` custom-driver definition needed for the
# built-in name, but the driver still must be enabled via `git config merge.ours.driver true` in
# whatever repo/clone runs the merge — this is a per-clone git config, not a versioned file, so
# operators and the drop-in check's --selftest must set it explicitly).
.foundry/build-provenance.yaml merge=ours
